IMPORT prelude
IMPORT properties

-- D1, naive: Alice buys on the belief her check left. WRONG ON PURPOSE.
--
-- Alice and Bob each mean to buy dinner tonight, and neither wants to buy
-- it if the other already has. This file models Alice's side; Bob's
-- purchase is the environment's act, recorded by the dinner ledger. Alice
-- checks whether dinner is bought, and if her check said it was open she
-- buys, without asking again. If Bob's purchase is recorded between her
-- check and her purchase, two dinners are bought. That is the race, and
-- this design does nothing about it: P1 is violated, by the three steps
-- check, Bob's purchase, buy (the traces at the end). Do not fix it; see
-- README.md.
--
-- The model is the brief's, transition for transition (README.md has the
-- table). One chain, one acting party, World, and each act names its
-- actor (REGULATIVE-LOWERING-SPEC.md section 4.3, option C). Every act is
-- a permission, so the chain is a MAY at every point, which is the shape
-- option C is sound for. A transition's guard is the PROVIDED of the
-- permission: an act whose guard is false is passed over and changes
-- nothing. Its effect is the CONSIDER under HENCE. The six variables are
-- ledger cells (properties.l4 lists them).
--
-- Times are seconds after midnight: the arrangement opens at 18:00
-- (64800) and closes at 21:00 (75600). The brief's model is untimed;
-- the closing time only ends each trace.

DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    `ledger records Bob's purchase`            -- BobBuys
    `Messages delivers the message`            -- Deliver
    `Alice checks whether dinner is bought`    -- CheckBought
    `Alice is done`                            -- Done
    `Alice buys dinner`                        -- Buy
    `Alice gives up`                           -- Abandon

`closing` MEANS 75600

§ `D1: the guards`

GIVEN act IS AN Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the brief allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `ledger records Bob's purchase`         THEN `the ledger is open` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
    WHEN `Messages delivers the message`         THEN (RECALL Messages's `message`) EQUALS JUST `in transit`
    WHEN `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS planning
    WHEN `Alice is done`                         THEN `Alice has bought or stopped` (RECALL Alice's `plan`)
    WHEN `Alice buys dinner`                     THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS checked
                                                      AND (RECALL Alice's `belief`) EQUALS JUST opened
    WHEN `Alice gives up`                        THEN `where Alice is` (RECALL Alice's `plan`) EQUALS checked
                                                      AND (RECALL Alice's `belief`) EQUALS JUST taken

§ `D1: the arrangement`

-- The arrangement opens with dinner unbought: the ledger's first record.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the arrangement` MEANS
    COMMIT `dinner status record` IS opened
    HENCE `the evening`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`the evening` MEANS
    PARTY World
    MAY   act PROVIDED `the brief allows` act
    WITHIN 0 OF closing
    HENCE CONSIDER act
          WHEN `ledger records Bob's purchase` THEN
              COMMIT `dinner status record` IS taken
              HENCE RECORD Messages's `message` IS `in transit`
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Messages delivers the message` THEN
              RECORD Messages's `message` IS delivered
              HENCE RECORD Alice's `belief` IS taken
              HENCE `Alice stops unless she has bought` (RECALL Alice's `plan`)
          WHEN `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` THEN
              RECORD Alice's `belief` IS `the ledger's status` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
              HENCE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS checked
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice is done` THEN `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice buys dinner` THEN
              COMMIT `dinners bought` IS `dinner for two`
              HENCE COMMIT `open at acceptance` IS `the ledger is open` (RECALL ALL OFFICIAL's `dinner status record`)
              HENCE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS bought
              HENCE `the evening`
          WHEN `Alice gives up` THEN
              RECORD Alice's `plan` IS stopped
              HENCE `the evening`
    LEST  FULFILLED

-- The message stops Alice if she is still on her way to buying.
GIVEN plan IS A MAYBE Plan
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`Alice stops unless she has bought` MEANS
    IF `Alice has bought or stopped` plan
    THEN `the evening`
    ELSE RECORD Alice's `plan` IS stopped
         HENCE `the evening`

§ `D1: the traces`

-- Read each trace's ledgers, not its FULFILLED line: every trace ends
-- FULFILLED, because the evening is a permission that lapses at closing.
-- The official record lists the dinner ledger's COMMITs in the order they
-- happened, so a bad purchase shows as `taken` before `dinners bought`,
-- followed by `open at acceptance IS FALSE`.

-- The counterexample, three steps: Alice checks at 18:05 and finds dinner
-- open; Bob's purchase is recorded at 18:06; Alice buys at 18:07 on what
-- her check told her. Official record: opened, taken, dinner for two,
-- open at acceptance FALSE. P1 is violated.
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY World DOES `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` AT 65100
    PARTY World DOES `ledger records Bob's purchase`         AT 65160
    PARTY World DOES `Alice buys dinner`                     AT 65220
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 75601)

-- Sequence A in full: the same three steps, then the message "I bought
-- it" reaches Alice at 18:08, too late to stop her. Her belief becomes
-- taken; her plan stays bought. Same official record as above.
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY World DOES `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` AT 65100
    PARTY World DOES `ledger records Bob's purchase`         AT 65160
    PARTY World DOES `Alice buys dinner`                     AT 65220
    PARTY World DOES `Messages delivers the message`         AT 65280
    PARTY World DOES `Alice is done`                         AT 65290
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 75601)

-- Sequence B: Alice buys at 18:05:30, before Bob's purchase is recorded.
-- Official record: opened, dinner for two, open at acceptance TRUE, taken.
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY World DOES `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` AT 65100
    PARTY World DOES `Alice buys dinner`                     AT 65130
    PARTY World DOES `ledger records Bob's purchase`         AT 65160
    PARTY World DOES `Messages delivers the message`         AT 65280
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 75601)

-- Alice checks after Bob's purchase is recorded: her check says taken, so
-- the purchase at 18:07 is passed over (its guard is false) and she gives
-- up. No dinner of hers is recorded.
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY World DOES `ledger records Bob's purchase`         AT 65160
    PARTY World DOES `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` AT 65190
    PARTY World DOES `Alice buys dinner`                     AT 65220
    PARTY World DOES `Alice gives up`                        AT 65230
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 75601)

-- Guards: a purchase before any check, a second purchase of Bob's, and a
-- second message are all passed over. Then the message stops Alice before
-- she has checked, and her late check is passed over too.
#TRACE `the arrangement` AT 64800 WITH
    PARTY World DOES `Alice buys dinner`                     AT 65000
    PARTY World DOES `ledger records Bob's purchase`         AT 65160
    PARTY World DOES `ledger records Bob's purchase`         AT 65170
    PARTY World DOES `Messages delivers the message`         AT 65280
    PARTY World DOES `Messages delivers the message`         AT 65290
    PARTY World DOES `Alice checks whether dinner is bought` AT 65300
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 75601)
